I'm thinking about how T3 decides to keep control of the near side and manage resource access. It seems like refusing to give up the whole system causes arguments. The vices could include injustice and possessiveness, although they aren't clearly named in traditional lists. Many traditions link virtues with their opposites, like injustice in some and justice in others. I wonder if I could label these as "injustice/partiality," borrowing from different perspectives. I’ll quote, "I keep the near side" to emphasize this stance.**Reflecting on fairness and gatekeeping**

